---
import {CodeTabs} from '../dmf-ui/code-tabs';
import {CodeSnippet} from '../dmf-ui/code-block';
import {LoadingButton} from '../dmf-ui/loading-button';
const sizes=[['xs','1.5rem','24px','12px'],['sm','1.75rem','28px','16px'],['default / md','2rem','32px','16px'],['lg','2.25rem','36px','16px']];
const figma=[['Size','Variant: xs, sm, default/md, lg; separate icon sizes','Same size strings in Astro and React; md is an alias'],['Variant','Variant: default, secondary, outline, ghost, destructive, link','variant in both adapters; no primary rename'],['State','Default, hover, active, focus-visible, disabled; prototype transient interactions','Native/CSS states; disabled is a real attribute'],['Leading / trailing icon','Boolean visibility plus icon instance swap for each slot','Authored Astro slot content or React children; decorative aria-hidden'],['Icon only','Explicit content configuration; keep a meaningful label property','icon/icon-xs/icon-sm/icon-lg plus aria-label'],['Label','Text property','Astro slot or React children'],['Width','Auto Layout Hug or Fill, independent of Size','class="w-full" / className="w-full"'],['Pending','LoadingButton composition, not a second Button state prop','Astro LoadingButton + setLoadingButtonState; React host owns async state']];
---
<section class="docs-section docs-prose" id="button-architecture" data-button-architecture>
  <h2>Button architecture</h2>
  <p>The anatomy is a native action, optional leading icon, label and optional trailing icon. Width, visual variant, size and authored content are independent. A navigation action uses an anchor with a real destination.</p>
  <h3>Compact sizes and mobile use</h3>
  <div class="docs-table-scroll"><table class="docs-options"><thead><tr><th>Size</th><th>Height</th><th>At 16px root</th><th>Default icon</th></tr></thead><tbody>{sizes.map(row=><tr>{row.map(cell=><td><code>{cell}</code></td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>Square icon sizes are icon-xs, icon-sm, icon and icon-lg, with the same 24/28/32/36px scale. Author icons without a fixed size to inherit those defaults. Explicit icon classes can override them. The browser text root and zoom still scale rem values.</p>
  <p>The earlier 28/32/40/48/56px proposal is a different scale. No existing consumer requires it, so this milestone keeps the compact defaults and does not add XL. A future comfortable profile should be explicit and opt-in, with separately verified spacing, typography and icon values. Never enlarge every control automatically on mobile. Assess target spacing and task context separately from visual height.</p>
  <h3>Variants, content and navigation</h3>
  <p>Default is the filled primary action. Secondary, outline and ghost vary emphasis; destructive signals a dangerous action. Link changes appearance while retaining the underlying element's semantics. A link-looking button still performs an action; an anchor navigates.</p>
  <p>The configurator above provides an actual local action with each content placement. Icon-only controls need a stable accessible name; tooltip/title text is supplementary. Hover, active and focus-visible come from CSS and user input, not forced visual-state props. Disabled prevents native activation; it is distinct from pending.</p>
  <CodeTabs id="button-adapter-examples" label="Button adapter examples" items={[
    {value:'astro',label:'Astro',language:'astro',title:'ButtonExample.astro',code:`---\nimport {Button} from 'dmf-ui/button';\nimport {Search} from '@lucide/astro';\n---\n<Button type="submit" variant="outline" size="md" class="w-full">\n  <Search aria-hidden="true" /> Search\n</Button>\n<Button href="/components/" variant="link">Browse components</Button>`},
    {value:'react',label:'React',language:'tsx',title:'ButtonExample.tsx',code:`import {useRef} from 'react';\nimport {Button} from '@dmf-ui/react';\nimport {buttonVariants} from 'dmf-ui/button/variants';\n\nexport function Example() {\n  const action = useRef<HTMLButtonElement>(null);\n  return <>\n    <Button ref={action} type="submit" variant="outline" size="md" className="w-full">Search</Button>\n    <a href="/components/" className={buttonVariants({variant:'link'})}>Browse components</a>\n  </>;\n}`}
  ]}/>
  <p>Astro Button defaults to button with type=button, or infers an anchor when href is present; as can explicitly select an element. Native submit/reset behavior requires the corresponding type and a form. React Button renders only a native button, forwards its ref and onClick/native attributes, and accepts children. React navigation uses an authored anchor with the shared variant function. Do not invent React href/as support or disabled-anchor behavior.</p>
  <h3>Pending behavior</h3>
  <p>Reuse the existing Astro LoadingButton. It disables duplicate activation, exposes aria-busy, reserves space for both labels and keeps the visible action label and accessible name stable. Its separate status region announces loadingLabel; the host announces completion/failure and finishes/cancels its own work. Reduced motion removes spinner rotation. SSR loading=true already renders disabled; authored disabled stays disabled when pending ends.</p>
  <LoadingButton label="Save draft" loadingLabel="Saving draft…" loading presentation="icon-label"/>
  <CodeSnippet title="Pending action" language="ts" code={`import {setLoadingButtonState} from 'dmf-ui/loading-button';\n\nsetLoadingButtonState(button, true);\ntry {\n  await saveDraft(); // Host-owned operation.\n  status.textContent = 'Draft saved.';\n} catch {\n  status.textContent = 'Save failed. Try again.';\n} finally {\n  setLoadingButtonState(button, false);\n}`}/>
  <p>There is no React LoadingButton export. A React host can combine disabled, aria-busy, a stable aria-label, reserved label width and role=status with its own async state. Preserve that distinction rather than adding a second loading runtime.</p>
  <h3>Tokens and Figma mapping</h3>
  <p>Foundations own control-height-xs/sm/md/lg. Button aliases own height-xs/sm/default/lg, default horizontal padding and gap. Existing semantic primary/secondary/destructive/background/foreground roles own fills and text; border, ring and radius own boundaries and focus. Typography remains the compact text-sm/font-medium scale (text-xs at XS), icons inherit the size variant, and disabled opacity stays .5. Loading reuses Button variants and the existing reduced-motion spinner. Presets change roles, not Button logic.</p>
  <p><a href="/docs/foundation-spacing/">Inspect shared control sizing under Foundations</a>. Changing a component alias is an explicit application override; it never silently chooses a mobile profile.</p>
  <div class="docs-table-scroll"><table class="docs-options"><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Figma specification</th><th>Code mapping</th></tr></thead><tbody>{figma.map(row=><tr>{row.map(cell=><td>{cell}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>Create dedicated visual variants for supported size, emphasis and relevant state combinations. Use booleans and instance swaps for icons and Auto Layout for width; do not multiply the component set for every label, icon or viewport. Prototype hover/press/focus transitions and show a separate disabled reference. This specification creates no Figma file.</p>
  <h3>Compatibility and accessibility</h3>
  <p>All existing size/variant names remain. Default and md have identical classes and geometry. No primary alias, XL size, universal loading prop or fullWidth prop is added. Full width remains an authored layout class. LoadingButton now keeps its action label visible and its accessible name stable; loadingLabel moves to a separate status announcement so the visible label stays in the accessible name.</p>
  <p>Keep native keyboard activation and visible focus, give forms associated errors, and use real destinations for links. CB and HUI retain the owner's white primary labels: approximately 2.57:1 and 4.29:1 on the unchanged base fills. These are not WCAG AA normal-text passes. An accessible alternative can use the outline variant or an explicitly approved higher-contrast action pairing; do not silently change the brand fill or label policy.</p>
</section>
